# <sha1> <relpath> — oracle gate
#
# NOTE: byte-exact / relocation-aware gating is NOT applicable to liero-dos.
# The build target is a Free Pascal -Mtp Linux x86-64 ELF (build/liero-dos),
# while the original is a 16-bit real-mode DOS MZ EXE (liero.exe). The binary
# formats are fundamentally different, so no relpath can pass byte-exact or
# relocation-aware comparison.
#
# The verification gate for liero-dos is dat-parity (engine/verify.py --oracle
# dat-parity), which runs the DAT parse/serialize selftest (always) plus a
# LIERO.DAT round-trip when extracted/liero-dos/LIERO.DAT is present (BYOD).
# The selftest passes; LIERO.DAT is not currently in the BYOD extraction, so
# round-trip coverage is 0% until the DAT file is extracted.
#
# Per-function oracle matching is handled by tools/e6_match.py (CFG + mnemonic
# histogram comparison against Ghidra asm). See reports/overnight6/ for results.
